# Optimization Benchmark Lineage

For any change intended to improve tokens, cost, latency, output size, or model
turn count:

1. Record a correctness-gated baseline before implementation.
2. Append the result to `benchmarks/results/optimization-lineage.md`; never
   replace an older stage.
3. Record provider, exact model, thinking level, task-set fingerprint, fixture
   commit, repetitions, binary/commit hash, and raw run directories.
4. Report both immediate delta from the parent stage and cumulative delta from
   the original comparable baseline.
5. Preserve every per-task regression even when aggregate metrics improve.
6. Compare only matching scope fingerprints. Keep targeted experiments in a
   separate lineage from full-suite results.
7. Do not claim savings from failed or correctness-ungated runs.
8. Update `benchmarks/optimization-lineage.json`, then sync it into
   `~/.daimonos/benchmarks.db` with `benchmarks/benchmark_db.py`.
